{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_ns_surreal_bridge","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.qou_ns_surreal_bridge","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Logic.Basic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.internal_regular_of_classical_regular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.internal_regular_of_classical_regular","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L153-L163","doc":"**Contrapositive.** If the standard-part classical flow is Leray–Hopf\nregular, then the QOU's internal q-NS is not singular — so no genuine QOU\n(whose internal flow is singular) can have a regular standard-part flow\n*under this bridge*. This is the honest statement of what closing B2 would\nrequire. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.classical_singular_of_internal_blowup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.classical_singular_of_internal_blowup","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L140-L151","doc":"**Transport, given the surreal bridge.** If the QOU's internal q-NS is\nsingular, then the standard-part classical flow is *not* Leray–Hopf regular.\nA one-line consequence of the two B2 halves — the difficulty is entirely in\nthe open hypothesis `classical_regular_iff_finite`. Compose with\n`qou_internal_ns_singular` (given a QOU, `internalBlowup` holds) to conclude:\n*given a QOU + the surreal bridge, the classical flow is singular.* ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.classical_regular_iff_finite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.classical_regular_iff_finite","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L136-L136","doc":"**The analytic wall (OPEN):** classical `L²` Leray–Hopf regularity ⟺ the\nsurreal observable is finite. All the analysis is here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.blowup_iff_infinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.blowup_iff_infinite","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L133-L133","doc":"**Surreal side (`surreal-blowup-calculus`, in-corpus):** internal blow-up ⟺\nthe observable is an *infinite* surreal (no finite standard part). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.classicalRegular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.classicalRegular","kind":"def","line":130,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L130-L130","doc":"Leray–Hopf regularity of the standard-part flow in `L²(ℝ³)` (the classical\nobject — Object 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.internalBlowup","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.internalBlowup","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L127-L127","doc":"The QOU's internal q-NS singularity observable (`ns-obstruction-tower`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.isFinite","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.isFinite","kind":"def","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L125-L125","doc":"\"`x` is a finite surreal\" — has a standard part `st x ∈ ℝ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.internalObs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.internalObs","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L123-L123","doc":"The surreal-valued internal q-NS observable at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge.mk","kind":"ctor","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L121-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.QOUNSSurrealBridge","kind":"structure","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/qou_ns_surreal_bridge.lean#L115-L136","doc":"Bridge B2, factored through the standard-part functor `st : S → ℝ`.\n\n`internalObs : S` is the surreal-valued QOU-internal q-NS observable at\n`q = 1` (e.g. the enstrophy / obstruction magnitude); `isFinite` marks the\nsurreals with a well-defined standard part. The two biconditionals are the\ntwo halves of B2; the second is the open analytic wall. ","signatureChunk":0}]}